<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>AXIA News Tracker — Markets / Trading Desk</title><id>https://axia-enterprises-dev.github.io/news-tracker/feeds/markets.xml</id><link rel="self" href="https://axia-enterprises-dev.github.io/news-tracker/feeds/markets.xml"/><link href="https://axia-enterprises-dev.github.io/news-tracker/"/><updated>2026-10-20T06:42:02.168671+00:00</updated><entry><title>McBride seeks increased buyback authority at upcoming AGM</title><link href="https://www.investing.com/news/company-news/mcbride-seeks-increased-buyback-authority-at-upcoming-agm-93CH-4958828"/><id>urn:nt:4d7d86bbe3949b</id><updated>2026-10-20T06:03:04+00:00</updated><summary></summary><author><name>All News</name></author><category term="business"/><category term="markets"/></entry><entry><title>Tonbo Imaging’s Rs 852 crore IPO subscribed 140x. Check GMP, allotment, other details</title><link href="https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/ipos/fpos/tonbo-imagings-rs-852-crore-ipo-subscribed-140x-check-gmp-allotment-other-details/articleshow/135062276.cms"/><id>urn:nt:7bf931e1d4dc15</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:45:38+00:00</updated><summary>The issue received bids for 1,15,86,91,464 shares against 85,26,033 shares on offer. Qualified institutional buyers led the demand, subscribing to their allotted portion 293.56 times. The non-institutional investor category was subscribed 170.94 times, while the retail portion saw 31.06 times subscription.</summary><author><name>Economic Times</name></author><category term="business"/><category term="markets"/></entry><entry><title>Jio IPO’s GMP rises to 22% as India’s largest ever issue set to open on October 21. Should you subscribe?</title><link href="https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/ipos/fpos/jio-ipos-gmp-rises-to-22-as-indias-largest-ever-issue-set-to-open-on-october-21-should-you-subscribe/articleshow/135061297.cms"/><id>urn:nt:5c08833cce37b2</id><updated>2026-10-20T04:22:31+00:00</updated><summary>The IPO is priced at Rs 1,065-1,119 per share and will open on October 21, closing on October 23. At the upper end of the price band, the grey market premium points to an indicative listing price of Rs 1,364 per share.</summary><author><name>Economic Times</name></author><category term="business"/><category term="markets"/></entry><entry><title>OpenAI races to lock in $30B at $1.4Tvaluation ahead of Anthropic IPO</title><link href="https://seekingalpha.com/news/4654452-openai-races-to-lock-in-30b-at-14tvaluation-ahead-of-anthropic-ipo?utm_source=feed_news_all&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;feed_item_type=news"/><id>urn:nt:4ded6ecd326fc5</id><updated>2026-10-20T04:15:20+00:00</updated><summary></summary><author><name>Seeking Alpha Market Currents</name></author><category term="markets"/><category term="ai"/><category term="markets"/></entry><entry><title>Jio IPO vs Airtel shares: Which telecom giant offers greater valuation comfort to investors?</title><link href="https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/ipos/fpos/jio-ipo-vs-airtel-shares-which-telecom-giant-offers-greater-valuation-comfort-to-investors/articleshow/135053174.cms"/><id>urn:nt:3cefb853da3c20</id><updated>2026-10-20T04:00:00+00:00</updated><summary>The Rs 30,213-crore public offering comprises an entirely fresh issue of 27 crore shares. If completed as planned, it will become India’s largest-ever initial public offering (IPO), surpassing Hyundai Motor India’s record set in 2024.</summary><author><name>Economic Times</name></author><category term="business"/><category term="markets"/></entry><entry><title>Metaplanet Turns an Esports Veteran Into a Bitcoin Treasury Giant</title><link href="https://news.bitcoin.com/featured/metaplanet-turns-an-esports-veteran-into-a-bitcoin-treasury-giant/"/><id>urn:nt:7c34882b51cda6</id><updated>2026-10-20T03:30:40+00:00</updated><summary>Super League shareholders just cleared the way for a gaming company to become a bitcoin treasury heavyweight, courtesy of 2,100 BTC from Japan’s Meta